From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:32:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: sun4i-usb: Write the A733 PHY0 control bits while the
 PHY is in reset

Without this, USB0 of the A733 never works as a gadget: the MUSB
reports no VBUS (DEVCTL VBUS bits 00) and the host sees no device.

The PHY takes the control bits of PHYCTL, here VBUSVLDEXT and SIDDQ,
only when its reset is released. The driver wrote them after the
release, and the reset is already released when the kernel starts, so
the PHY never saw them. Add an A733 match with the D1 configuration
and a flag that asserts the PHY reset, writes the bits and releases the
reset again. Other SoCs are unchanged.

The manual gives no minimum time for the PHY reset; the 10 ms are not
measured as one.

Not covered: PHY1, which works with the existing order.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: with the D1 compatible alone the gadget
never enumerates on J16; pulsing the PHY reset after the driver has
written PHYCTL makes DEVCTL report VBUS and the gadget enumerate.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the Type-C port J16 on a host, the USB0
gadget enumerates at high speed after a cold start, also with the plug
turned over, and the hub on USB1 still enumerates.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
index e2fbf8ccf99e..b265674644da 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@ struct sun4i_usb_phy_cfg {
 	bool phy0_dual_route;
 	bool needs_phy2_siddq;
 	bool siddq_in_base;
+	bool phyctl_in_reset;
 	bool poll_vbusen;
 	int missing_phys;
 };
@@ -270,6 +271,26 @@ static int sun4i_usb_phy_init(struct phy *_phy)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The A733 PHY0 takes its control bits only when its reset is
+	 * released, so hold it in reset while they are written.
+	 */
+	if (data->cfg->phyctl_in_reset && phy->index == 0) {
+		ret = reset_control_assert(phy->reset);
+		if (ret) {
+			clk_disable_unprepare(phy->clk2);
+			clk_disable_unprepare(phy->clk);
+			return ret;
+		}
+
+		usleep_range(10000, 11000);
+
+		val = readl(data->base + data->cfg->phyctl_offset);
+		val |= PHY_CTL_VBUSVLDEXT;
+		val &= ~PHY_CTL_SIDDQ;
+		writel(val, data->base + data->cfg->phyctl_offset);
+	}
+
 	ret = reset_control_deassert(phy->reset);
 	if (ret) {
 		clk_disable_unprepare(phy->clk2);
@@ -987,6 +1008,15 @@ static const struct sun4i_usb_phy_cfg sun20i_d1_cfg = {
 	.siddq_in_base = true,
 };
 
+static const struct sun4i_usb_phy_cfg sun60i_a733_cfg = {
+	.phyctl_offset = REG_PHYCTL_A33,
+	.dedicated_clocks = true,
+	.hci_phy_ctl_clear = PHY_CTL_SIDDQ,
+	.phy0_dual_route = true,
+	.siddq_in_base = true,
+	.phyctl_in_reset = true,
+};
+
 static const struct sun4i_usb_phy_cfg sun50i_a64_cfg = {
 	.disc_thresh = 3,
 	.phyctl_offset = REG_PHYCTL_A33,
@@ -1029,6 +1059,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id sun4i_usb_phy_of_match[] = {
 	  .data = &sun50i_a64_cfg},
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-usb-phy", .data = &sun50i_h6_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-usb-phy", .data = &sun50i_h616_cfg },
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb-phy",
+	  .data = &sun60i_a733_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,suniv-f1c100s-usb-phy",
 	  .data = &suniv_f1c100s_cfg },
 	{ },
